Patch 7932 (experiment, present path): PRESENT_TEAR=1 and WAITABLE_SC=<1-3>, both off by default.

PRESENT_TEAR=1: in the default present mode (no vblank wait) the swap chain is made with ALLOW_TEARING when DXGI supports it and
Present passes DXGI_PRESENT_ALLOW_TEARING (Microsoft's advice for windowed and borderless flip-model games: a borderless window that
owns the screen can use independent flip and VRR). A composed window looks as before; an independently flipped one can tear.
D3D12_VSYNC=1 never passes it (sync interval 1). After creation the swap chain's real flags (GetDesc1) decide: no ALLOW_TEARING flag,
no ALLOW_TEARING present (it would be DXGI_ERROR_INVALID_CALL). D3D12_VSYNC=0 keeps working as before.
WAITABLE_SC=n: the swap chain gets FRAME_LATENCY_WAITABLE_OBJECT and SetMaximumFrameLatency(n); the thread that presents (the submit
thread with PIPE=1) waits on the object before it records a batch that presents, bounded at 100 ms. It is the wait Present would do,
earlier; the HITCH probe counts it under "Present", and a line every 1800 presents gives the total and the timeouts. A timed-out
wait is taken back with zero-timeout waits on later presents, so one long hitch does not raise the latency for the rest of the run.
With GPU_OVERLAP=1, WAITABLE_SC=1 is raised to 2 (logged): latency 1 would hold the submit thread until the previous batch was
shown, which is the drain the overlap removes. Start lines:
"[D3D12] present flags: ..." and "[D3D12] WAITABLE_SC=n: frame-latency object on". Nothing the guest reads changes.

